#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "</AccordionItem>\n"
#| "</Accordion>\n"
#| "The reference primitives in the Qiskit SDK perform local statevector simulations. These simulations do not support\n"
#| "modeling device noise, but are useful for quickly prototyping algorithms before looking into more advanced simulation\n"
#| "techniques ([using Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits)) or running on real devices ([Qiskit Runtime primitives](primitives)).\n"
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"The reference primitives in the Qiskit SDK perform local statevector simulations. These simulations do not support\n"
"modeling device noise, but are useful for quickly prototyping algorithms before looking into more advanced simulation\n"
"techniques ([using Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits)) or running on real devices ([IBM Quantum primitives](primitives)).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Ang mga reference primitives sa Qiskit SDK ay nagsasagawa ng lokal na statevector simulations. Hindi sinusuportahan ng mga simulation na ito ang\n"
"pag-modelo ng noise ng device, ngunit kapaki-pakinabang para sa mabilis na pag-prototype ng mga algorithm bago tumingin sa mas advanced na mga teknik sa simulation\n"
"([gamit ang Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits)) o pagpapatakbo sa mga tunay na device ([Qiskit Runtime primitives](primitives)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Estimator primitive can compute expectation values of circuits, and the Sampler primitive can sample\n"
"from output distributions of circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Estimator primitive ay maaaring mag-compute ng mga expectation value ng mga circuit, at ang Sampler primitive ay maaaring mag-sample\n"
"mula sa mga output distribution ng mga circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following sections show how to use the reference primitives to run your workflow locally.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng mga sumusunod na seksyon kung paano gamitin ang mga reference primitives para patakbuhin ang iyong workflow nang lokal.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the reference Estimator {#use-the-reference-estimator}"
msgstr "Gamitin ang reference Estimator {#use-the-reference-estimator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The reference implementation of `EstimatorV2` in `qiskit.primitives` that runs on a local statevector\n"
"simulators is the [`StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator) class. It can take circuits, observables, and parameters as inputs and returns the locally computed expectation values.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang reference implementation ng `EstimatorV2` sa `qiskit.primitives` na tumatakbo sa lokal na statevector\n"
"simulators ay ang [`StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator) class. Maaari itong tumanggap ng mga circuit, observable, at parameter bilang input at ibinabalik ang mga lokal na kinomputang expectation value.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code prepares the inputs that will be used in the examples that follow. The expected input type for the\n"
"observables is [`qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp). Note that\n"
"the circuit in the example is parametrized, but you can also run Estimator on non-parametrized circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inihahanda ng sumusunod na code ang mga input na gagamitin sa mga halimbawang susunod. Ang inaasahang uri ng input para sa\n"
"mga observable ay [`qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp). Tandaan na\n"
"ang circuit sa halimbawa ay may parameter, ngunit maaari ka ring magpatakbo ng Estimator sa mga circuit na walang parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Any circuit passed to an Estimator must **not** include any **measurements**.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Anumang circuit na ipinasa sa Estimator ay **hindi** dapat magsama ng anumang **measurements**.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/5b41a52d-8f15-4ce4-b3f6-effd91946d9c-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/5b41a52d-8f15-4ce4-b3f6-effd91946d9c-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Transpile to ISA circuits and observables\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Transpile to ISA circuits and observables\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "  The Qiskit Runtime primitives workflow requires circuits and observables to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as *instruction set architecture (ISA)* circuits and observables). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgid "  The IBM Quantum primitives workflow requires circuits and observables to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as *instruction set architecture (ISA)* circuits and observables). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgstr "  Ang Qiskit Runtime primitives workflow ay nangangailangan ng mga circuit at observable na ma-transform para gamitin lamang ang mga instruction na sinusuportahan ng QPU (tinatawag na *instruction set architecture (ISA)* circuits at observables). Ang mga reference primitives ay tumatanggap pa rin ng mga abstract na instruction, dahil umaasa sila sa lokal na statevector simulations, ngunit ang pag-transpile ng circuit ay maaari pa ring maging kapaki-pakinabang sa mga tuntunin ng pag-optimize ng circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize Estimator {#initialize-estimator}"
msgstr "I-initialize ang Estimator {#initialize-estimator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instantiate a [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator).\n"
msgstr "Mag-instantiate ng [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run and get results {#run-and-get-results}"
msgstr "Patakbuhin at kunin ang mga resulta {#run-and-get-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example only uses one circuit (of type [`QuantumCircuit`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)) and one\n"
"observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang halimbawang ito ay gumagamit lamang ng isang circuit (ng uri [`QuantumCircuit`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)) at isang\n"
"observable.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the estimation by calling the [`StatevectorEstimator.run`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator#run) method, which returns an instance of a [`PrimitiveJob`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob) object. You can get the results from the job (as a [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult) object)\n"
"with the [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob.result`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob#result) method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Patakbuhin ang estimation sa pamamagitan ng pagtawag sa [`StatevectorEstimator.run`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorEstimator#run) method, na nagbabalik ng instance ng [`PrimitiveJob`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob) object. Maaari mong makuha ang mga resulta mula sa job (bilang [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult) object)\n"
"gamit ang [`qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob.result`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveJob#result) method.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the expected value from the result {#get-the-expected-value-from-the-result}"
msgstr "Kunin ang expected value mula sa resulta {#get-the-expected-value-from-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The primitives result outputs an array of [`PubResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#pubresult) objects, where each item of the array is a `PubResult` object that contains in its data the array of evaluations corresponding to every circuit-observable combination in the PUB.\n"
msgstr "Ang output ng primitives result ay isang array ng mga [`PubResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#pubresult) object, kung saan ang bawat item ng array ay isang `PubResult` object na naglalaman sa data nito ng array ng mga evaluation na tumutugma sa bawat kombinasyon ng circuit-observable sa PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To retrieve the expectation values and metadata for the first (and in this case, only) circuit evaluation, we must access the evaluation [`data`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#data) for PUB 0:\n"
msgstr "Para makuha ang mga expectation value at metadata para sa unang (at sa kasong ito, tanging) circuit evaluation, dapat nating i-access ang evaluation [`data`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult#data) para sa PUB 0:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set Estimator run options {#set-estimator-run-options}"
msgstr "I-set ang mga run option ng Estimator {#set-estimator-run-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, the reference Estimator performs an exact statevector calculation based on the\n"
"[`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) class.\n"
"However, this can be modified to introduce the effect of the sampling overhead (also known as \"shot noise\").\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa default, ang reference Estimator ay nagsasagawa ng eksaktong statevector calculation batay sa\n"
"[`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) class.\n"
"Gayunpaman, maaari itong baguhin para ipakilala ang epekto ng sampling overhead (kilala rin bilang \"shot noise\").\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimator accepts a `precision` argument that expresses the error bars that the\n"
"primitive implementation should target for expectation values estimates.  This is the sampling overhead and is defined exclusively in the `.run()` method. This  lets you fine-tune the option all the way to the PUB level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tumatanggap ang Estimator ng `precision` argument na nagpapahayag ng mga error bar na dapat target ng\n"
"primitive implementation para sa mga estimate ng expectation value. Ito ang sampling overhead at eksklusibong tinukoy sa `.run()` method. Pinapayagan ka nitong i-fine-tune ang opsyon hanggang sa antas ng PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a full example, see the [Estimator examples](/guides/estimator-examples) page.\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang kumpletong halimbawa, tingnan ang pahina ng [Estimator examples](/guides/estimator-examples).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the reference Sampler {#use-the-reference-sampler}"
msgstr "Gamitin ang reference Sampler {#use-the-reference-sampler}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference implementations of `SamplerV2` in `qiskit.primitives` is the [`StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler) class. It takes circuits and parameters as inputs and returns the results from sampling from the output probability distributions as a quasi-probability distribution of output states.\n"
msgstr "Ang reference implementations ng `SamplerV2` sa `qiskit.primitives` ay ang [`StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler) class. Tumatanggap ito ng mga circuit at parameter bilang input at ibinabalik ang mga resulta mula sa pag-sample ng mga output probability distribution bilang quasi-probability distribution ng mga output state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code prepares the inputs used in the examples that follow. Note that\n"
"these examples run a single parametrized circuit, but you can also run Sampler\n"
"on non-parametrized circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inihahanda ng sumusunod na code ang mga input na ginamit sa mga halimbawang susunod. Tandaan na\n"
"ang mga halimbawang ito ay nagpapatakbo ng isang parametrized na circuit, ngunit maaari ka ring magpatakbo ng Sampler\n"
"sa mga circuit na walang parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/d4c0ac3b-8e5b-4cde-bb26-256324982c2c-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-sdk-primitives/extracted-outputs/d4c0ac3b-8e5b-4cde-bb26-256324982c2c-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Any quantum circuit passed to a Sampler **must** include measurements.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Anumang quantum circuit na ipinasa sa Sampler ay **dapat** magsama ng measurements.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "  The Qiskit Runtime primitives workflow requires circuits to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as ISA circuits). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgid "  The IBM Quantum primitives workflow requires circuits to be transformed to only use instructions supported by the QPU (referred to as ISA circuits). The reference primitives still accept abstract instructions, as they rely on local statevector simulations, but transpiling the circuit might still be beneficial in terms of circuit optimization.\n"
msgstr "  Ang Qiskit Runtime primitives workflow ay nangangailangan ng mga circuit na ma-transform para gamitin lamang ang mga instruction na sinusuportahan ng QPU (tinatawag na ISA circuits). Ang mga reference primitives ay tumatanggap pa rin ng mga abstract na instruction, dahil umaasa sila sa lokal na statevector simulations, ngunit ang pag-transpile ng circuit ay maaari pa ring maging kapaki-pakinabang sa mga tuntunin ng pag-optimize ng circuit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize `SamplerV2` {#initialize-samplerv2}"
msgstr "I-initialize ang `SamplerV2` {#initialize-samplerv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instantiate [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler):\n"
msgstr "Mag-instantiate ng [`qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.StatevectorSampler):\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run and get results {#run-and-get-results-1}"
msgstr "Patakbuhin at kunin ang mga resulta {#run-and-get-results-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Primitives accept multiple PUBs as inputs, and each PUB gets its own result. Therefore, you can run different circuits with various parameter/observable combinations, and retrieve the PUB results:\n"
msgstr "Tinatanggap ng mga Primitive ang maramihang PUB bilang input, at ang bawat PUB ay may sariling resulta. Kaya naman, maaari kang magpatakbo ng iba't ibang circuit na may iba't ibang kombinasyon ng parameter/observable, at makuha ang mga PUB result:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the probability distribution or measurement outcome {#get-the-probability-distribution-or-measurement-outcome}"
msgstr "Kunin ang probability distribution o measurement outcome {#get-the-probability-distribution-or-measurement-outcome}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurement outcome samples are returned as **bitstrings** or **counts**. The bitstrings show the measurement outcomes, preserving the shot order in which they were measured. The Sampler result objects organize data in terms of their input circuits' classical register names, for compatibility with dynamic circuits.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga sample ng measurement outcome ay ibinabalik bilang **bitstrings** o **counts**. Ipinapakita ng mga bitstring ang mga measurement outcome, pinapanatili ang pagkakasunud-sunod ng shot kung kailan sila sinukat. Inoorganisa ng mga Sampler result object ang data batay sa mga pangalan ng classical register ng kanilang input circuit, para sa compatibility sa mga dynamic na circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The name of the classical register defaults to `\"meas\"`. This name will be used later to access the measurement bitstrings.\n"
" </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ang pangalan ng classical register ay default sa `\"meas\"`. Gagamitin ang pangalang ito sa ibaba para i-access ang mga measurement bitstring.\n"
" </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change run options {#change-run-options}"
msgstr "Baguhin ang mga run option {#change-run-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, the reference Sampler performs an exact statevector calculation based on the\n"
"[`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) class.\n"
"However, this can be modified to introduce the effect of the sampling overhead (also known as \"shot noise\"). To help manage this overhead, the Sampler interface accepts a `shots` argument that can be defined at the PUB level.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa default, ang reference Sampler ay nagsasagawa ng eksaktong statevector calculation batay sa\n"
"[`quantum_info.Statevector`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) class.\n"
"Gayunpaman, maaari itong baguhin para ipakilala ang epekto ng sampling overhead (kilala rin bilang \"shot noise\"). Para makatulong sa pamamahala ng overhead na ito, tinatanggap ng Sampler interface ang `shots` argument na maaaring tukuyin sa antas ng PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example assumes you have defined two circuits.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapalagay ng halimbawang ito na tinukoy mo ang dalawang circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a full example, see the [Sampler examples](/guides/sampler-examples) page.\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang kumpletong halimbawa, tingnan ang pahina ng [Sampler examples](/guides/sampler-examples).\n"

